{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"summary": "Declared the experiment before measuring. Question: for a file with one staged hunk and one unstaged hunk, does any shipped hook runner's formatter cause the unstaged hunk's content to reach the commit? Oracle: bytes of git show :app.js and git cat-file blob HEAD:app.js, no grading and no model. Population: lefthook, pre-commit, lint-staged, husky, and the plain git idiom. Strongest accessible alternative per runner: its own unstaged-change handling, plus git stash push --keep-index as the no-framework remedy. Positive control: C0, the naive hand-written hook, which must report a sweep or the run is void (F010). Kill gate: if no shipped runner sweeps and the corpus rows are the wrong evidence, the hazard is not a candidate. Read both corpus rows verbatim first: nextjs-app-template#95 inverts the record's claim (lefthook 2.x hides the unstaged half) and agent-orchestra#154's own review shows the hazard raised and the defense SUSTAINED in a hand-written hook."}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "milestone", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 6, "session": "2026-10-07-003-e047-test-with-a-byte-level-oracle-wheth", "ts": "2026-10-07T07:20:27+00:00"}
