{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"summary": "E047 first run: both controls behave as required -- C0 (naive hand-written hook) SWEEPS byte-exactly, so the harness can detect the hazard, and B0 (no hook) commits the bad spacing without the marker, so the fixture is what the experiment describes. Measured on real runners at current versions: pre-commit 4.6.2 is clean (its own default stash hides the unstaged half), and the plain git idiom git stash push --keep-index is clean, both committing the reformatted staged hunk and preserving the unstaged one. husky 9.1.7 sweeps, as the naive pattern predicts. Two arms unmeasured because this VM's git 2.25.1 is below lefthook's 2.31 and lint-staged's 2.32 minimums, so both refused to start -- which would have read as 'no sweep' for arms that never ran; git 2.56.0 is being built from source rather than leaving the central comparison unmeasured."}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "milestone", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 14, "session": "2026-10-07-003-e047-test-with-a-byte-level-oracle-wheth", "ts": "2026-10-07T07:48:03+00:00"}
