{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"summary": "E047 measured, recorded and closed. Nine arms on real runners at current versions, both controls correct: the hazard is real and byte-exact (the naive hook's commit contains a line that was never staged, and the file then reads as modified while its content is already committed) and NO shipped runner produces it. lefthook 2.1.17 hides unstaged changes with AND without stage_fixed; lint-staged 17.6.0 hides them with defaults AND with --no-stash; pre-commit 4.6.2 hides them around the hook by default; git stash push --keep-index prevents it with no framework at all. A2 and A5 run the same hook body one layer apart: husky supplies no staging and sweeps, pre-commit supplies its own and does not. Reading both corpus rows verbatim first inverted half the record: nextjs-app-template#95 exonerates lefthook, and agent-orchestra#154's own review records GH-1 'Defense sustained'. So the last observation derived from a candidate is closed with nothing to build. F083, D078. Three instrument defects recorded because each would have produced a wrong answer rather than an error, and one declared prediction (pre-commit would sweep) failed. The harness was split into five modules by invariant at the cap and the split verified behaviour-preserving: identical results.json in every arm field."}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "milestone", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 39, "session": "2026-10-07-003-e047-test-with-a-byte-level-oracle-wheth", "ts": "2026-10-07T08:21:23+00:00"}
